{"title":"2003 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, the value of x is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c2f8323c66979290f61b8f3fcad479b820d6de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 40 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 60 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 100 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 120 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"452\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can name the points to make everything easier to follow.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>we can see that angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e80c71d8f08383352a558a07cd96d6c6fa293f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DBC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> form a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">straight angle</a>, meaning we can set up an equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0abf4c1e8c9f2b40a6e2f5ae32012e65c351816e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle DBC + m\\angle ABC = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f293b1319a97a5c4ff617eda14acf9c8850c2e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 + m\\angle ABC = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"174\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d880e8691f32aa2145cd63301cbb0aeb07903532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC = 60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"119\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can now notice that angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0728bebb477a2636300c56851b6a6f9e382c1b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/84988ec15cf2e34af243bd6ea8b824f6cab1500d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ECF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertical_angles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vertical angles\">vertical angles</a>. This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2bbc2c7d160a5140cba42497b9f8464ac98774f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ACB = m\\angle ECF = 40^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"219\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We now have all of the angles of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The interior angles of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> always sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, allowing us to set up an equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bcb09b645cbb350c8b17eff1ff206722d378a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + m\\angle ACB + m\\angle ABC = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"251\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873fe0b5b0f99a698e3617dc25a2dede00748ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 60 + 40 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56066e80011315b18b0c4e40f6c1989bb96f58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 100 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b3ad9a5a5efa2d79e4ff9afb1738967817438f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 180 - 100 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"201\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202416\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 66/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1235/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2891/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.690      1 -total\n 72.06%    5.541      4 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:32570:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202416 and revision id 251627. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}